uring the year by an American author, preferably dealing with American ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d1\"},\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... Wodehouse) and The Voyage Out (Virginia Woolf).Haslam, Sara (13 October 2015), \\\"Ford's The Good Soldier Wins The Cheltenham Booker 1915 at 2015 Festival\\\". Ford Madox Oxford Society. Retrieved 27 November 2016.\\n\\nSee also\\n\\n* Baillie Gifford Prize (formerly the Samuel Johnson Prize)\\n* Commonwealth Writers Prize\\n* Costa Book ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"88cb342a6bae56107f683e2056cb8d1749adb200b202c1f3e49268fbfc7f2b88\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"b86a0c2efd0b1a90d7be55693ec320554b29545672b345939e587c013516a400\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Fishermen Chigozie Obioma Booker Prize shortlisted 2015 2016\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2019 | Winners | Bernardine Evaristo | Girl, Woman, Other | Hamish Hamilton | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz Calder *Xiaolu Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Lucy Ellmann | Ducks, Newburyport | Galley Beggar | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz Calder *Xiaolu Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Chigozie Obioma | An Orchestra of Minorities | Little ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... Booker Prize\\\") was established in 1969. Each year, a panel of judges decide the best novel of the year written in English and published in the United Kingdom or Ireland.\\n\\nNotable winners: Life of Pi by Yann Martel (2002); The Testaments by Margaret Atwood (2019)\\n\\n5. Neustadt International ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tckpublishing.com/prestigious-literature-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... Those examples are acceptable in an instrumental piece. There are also times when lyrics are sung, but sparingly, and only to enhance the production (such as in \\\"So Rare\\\" by the Jimmy Dorsey orchestra and in \\\"Unchained Melody\\\" by Les Baxter and his orchestra).\\n\\nMost of us love ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goldminemag.com/music-history/top-instrumental-songs-from-1950s-and-1960s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... He has collaborated with the American Composers Orchestra, . . . Imani Winds, . . . and the NDR Big Band . . . [His] concert music has received . . . an ASCAP Morton Gould Award and the International Society of Bassists Composition Contest Grand Prize. He is Assistant Professor of Composition at Stephen F. Austin State University in ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsfuse.org/308089/concert-review-boston-symphony-orchestras-coltrane-legacy-for-orchestra-an-evening-of-worthwhile-rethinkings/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d60\"},\"ref\":\"d60\",\"snippet\":\" ... Opera Houses of Dubai and Tokyo, Midwest Band and Orchestra Clinic, International Women's Brass Conference, International Trumpet Guild Conference, Co-Principal Trumpet (Verbier Festival Chamber Orchestra in Switzerland since 2008); Boston Symphony Orchestra, Milwaukee Symphony. BROADWAY: The Phantom of the Opera, West Side Story, An American in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.chicagoshakes.com/productions/illinoise/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d61\"},\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... His longer works include the Septology trilogy, the third volume of which was shortlisted for the international Booker prize in 2022.\\n\\nSeptology, which Fosse started during a pause from playwriting and after converting to Catholicism in 2013, is about an ageing painter, Asle, living alone on the south ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/oct/05/jon-fosse-wins-the-2023-nobel-prize-in-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... C Minor (Rachmaninoff) | Leopold Stokowski Additional Information |\\n\\n1929 | 2004 | Classical/Opera |\\n\\n| Piano Sonata No. 2, \\\"Concord Sonata\\\" (album) |\\n\\nJohn Kirkpatrick Additional Information |\\n\\n1948 | 2003 | Classical/Opera |\\n\\n| Pictures at an Exhibition (album) |\\n\\nRafael Kubelik, Chicago Symphony Orchestra, et.al. Additional Information |\\n\\n1951 | 2003 | Classical/Opera |\\n\\n| The Play of Dani\",\"title\":\"https://www.loc.gov/programs/national-recording-preservation-board/recording-registry/complete-national-recording-registry-listing/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book was the joint winner of the 2019 Booker Prize.\\n\\nNonfiction\\n\\nIn 2008, Atwood published Payback: Debt and the Shadow Side of Wealth, a collection of five lectures delivered as part of the Massey Lectures from October 12 to November 1, 2008. The book was released in ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d64\"},\"ref\":\"d64\",\"snippet\":\" ... Rahbee was an assistant at the Vienna State opera from 2002-2010. As part of his fellowship and residency at the 2003 Salzburg Festival, Dr. Rahbee was assistant conductor of the International Attergau Institute Orchestra, where he worked with members of the Vienna Philharmonic. He has been selected ... \",\"title\":\"https://music.washington.edu/events/2023-11-03/uw-symphony-rachel-lee-priday-violin\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"99b428f8692bb91b0e19eb5a4b7c45e58dd9c53ab78bd74f383683215f7357d9\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"d6403169eb027f369ba9e96c0b3121d27f5947a09cee510fee0caa98be5371bb\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"An Orchestra of Minorities Booker International Prize 2019\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_bd0056e2258549699b5ba68a"},{"content":"I have a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages.\n\nBut the Booker Prize was established in 1969, not the 2000s. The question says \"the award itself\" was created in the 2000s. Let me reconsider - the Man Booker International Prize was established in 2005. Let me check the details of the Booker Prize page and the Man Booker International Prize.\n\nAlso, I need to verify: \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" was published in 2019 and shortlisted for the 2019 Booker Prize. The 2019 Booker Prize was won jointly by Margaret Atwood (\"The Testaments\") and Bernardine Evaristo (\"Girl, Woman, Other\"). Let me check if this fits the pattern.\n\nLet me read the Booker Prize page to understand the award structure, and search for the Man Booker International Prize.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d1\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_65d26db25e1349a8b70377af","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize established 2005 history\", \"International Booker Prize created 2005 2016 reconfigured\", \"Bernardine Evaristo born city biography\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_634e22a9c1114da19be81f68","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d1\",\"document_chars\":27249,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"8ce61c1087f7e5edc11d95aa8c819ec764b2f8d2e4c5ab64aaa81fda45d083cf\",\"snapshot\":\"25e42c9d9629a06063929aefe4e8f050cac2c095d797b7476410c1a6fe277c5a\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Booker Prize - Wikipedia\\nauthor: Authority control databases National Germany United States France BnF data Czech Republic Israel\\ndate: 2001-10-18\\n---\\nname: The Booker Prize\\nawarded_for: Best work of sustained fiction of the year, written in English and published in the UK or Ireland\\nreward: £50, 000\\npresenter: Booker, McConnell Ltd (1969–2001), Man Group (2002–2019), Crankstart (2019 onwards)\\nlocation: Somerset House, Strand, London, England\\nyear: 1969\\nimagesize: 150px\\n\\nThe Booker Prize, formerly the Booker Prize for Fiction (1969–2001) and the Man Booker Prize (2002–2019), is a prestigious literary award conferred each year for the best single work of sustained fiction written in the English language, which was published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. The winner of the Booker Prize receives , as well as international publicity that usually leads to a significant sales boost. When the prize was created, only novels written by Commonwealth, Irish and South African (and later Zimbabwean) citizens were eligible to receive the prize; in 2014, eligibility was widened to any English-language novel—a change that proved controversial.\\n\\nA five-person panel consisting of authors, publishers and journalists, as well as politicians, actors, artists and musicians, is appointed by the Booker Prize Foundation each year to choose the winning book. Gaby Wood has been the chief executive of the Booker Prize Foundation since 2015.Gaby Wood at The Booker Prizes.Jennifer (20 April 2015), \\\"Booker Prize Foundation Hints at New Direction with Appointment of Gaby Wood as Literary Director\\\", Books Live, Sunday Times (South Africa).\\n\\nA high-profile literary award in British culture, the Booker Prize is greeted with anticipation and fanfare around the world. Literary critics have noted that it is a mark of distinction for authors to be selected for inclusion in the shortlist or to be nominated for the \\\"longlist\\\".\\n\\nA sister prize, the International Booker Prize, is awarded for a work of fiction translated into English and published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. Unlike the Booker Prize, short story collections are eligible for the International Booker Prize. The £50,000 prize money is split evenly between the author and translator of the winning novel.\\n\\nHistory and administration\\n\\nThe prize was established as the \\\"Booker Prize for Fiction\\\" after the company Booker, McConnell Ltd began sponsoring the event in 1969; it became commonly known as the \\\"Booker Prize\\\" or the \\\"Booker\\\". Jock Campbell, Charles Tyrrell and Tom Maschler were instrumental in establishing the prize.\\n\\nWhen administration of the prize was transferred to the Booker Prize Foundation in 2002, the title sponsor became the investment company Man Group, which opted to retain \\\"Booker\\\" as part of the official title of the prize. The foundation is an independent registered charity funded by the entire profits of Booker Prize Trading Ltd, of which it is the sole shareholder. The prize money awarded w\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_65d26db25e1349a8b70377af"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d1\"},\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... Unlike the Booker Prize, short story collections are eligible for the International Booker Prize. The £50,000 prize money is split evenly between the author and translator of the winning novel.\\n\\nHistory and administration\\n\\nThe prize was established as the \\\"Booker Prize for Fiction\\\" after the company Booker ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... They kept the name Booker when they created the new Man Booker International Prize, but dropped it for the Man Asia Literary Prize.\\n\\nIn Australia, we have The Australian/Vogel Award for an unpublished first manuscript: a collaboration between a newspaper and a health foods company. The effect ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d65\"},\"ref\":\"d65\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Man Group invested in the prize from 2005 to 2015 renaming it the Man Booker Prize and awarding it every two years. Previously, the Man Booker Prize accepted work from the Commonwealth, Zimbabwe, and Ireland, but from 2014 the international Prize was widened to accept any writing ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/the-most-prestigious-literary-awards-in-the-world.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Previously called the Man Booker Prize, it has been awarded since 1969.\\n\\nRecent Winner\\n\\nPrevious Winner (2023)\\n\\nInternational Booker Prize\\n\\nA counterpart to the Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize was established in 2005. Originally presented biennially, in 2016 it had become an annual occurrence. Awarded to a ... \",\"title\":\"https://rocketexpansion.com/book-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her work has won the Nobel Prize in Literature, two Scotiabank Giller Prizes, three Governor General's Literary Awards and the Man Booker International Prize. Her first book, Dance of the Happy Shades, was released in 1968, and she continued to write stories until retiring in 2013.\\n\\nWachtel ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... Coetzee | Slow Man | Secker & Warburg | *John Sutherland (chair) *Lindsay Duguid *Rick Gekoski *Josephine Hart *David Sexton |\\n| 2005 The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en |archive-date=10 December 2022 |archive-url= |url-status=live }} | Longlist | Rachel Cusk | In the Fold | Faber ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d66\"},\"ref\":\"d66\",\"snippet\":\" ... Julian Barnes (born 1946) is another successful living novelist, who won the 2011 Man Booker Prize for his book The Sense of an Ending, while three of his earlier books were shortlisted for the Booker Prize: Flaubert's Parrot (1984), England, England (1998), and Arthur & George (2005). He ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twentieth-century_English_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d67\"},\"ref\":\"d67\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1976\\n\\nSaul Bellow is awarded the Nobel Prize in Literature.\\n\\nAvery is founded and establishes itself as the most successful independent publisher of health books in the market.\\n\\n1978\\n\\nIris Murdoch's The Sea, The Sea (Penguin) is awarded the Booker Prize.\\n\\nDutton publishes John Irving's The ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.penguin.com/our-story-timeline/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... Coetzee, Hilary Mantel and Margaret Atwood.Man Booker official site: J. G. Farrell ; Hilary Mantel ; J. M. Coetzee: . Carey won his first Booker Prize in 1988, for Oscar and Lucinda, and won his second Booker Prize in 2001, for True History of the Kelly Gang.John Ezard, \\\"Carey ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Carey_(novelist)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... Prize for Fiction.)\\n* Oryx and Crake (2003, finalist for the 2003 Booker Prize and the 2003 Governor General's Award and shortlisted for the 2004 Orange Prize for Fiction.)\\n* The Penelopiad (2005, nominated for the 2006 Mythopoeic Fantasy Award for Adult Literature and longlisted for the 2007 International ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"8ed19ab26ac7b65980c5ad9ba1955d0dce2c854e9107e955e827e385bd16bb72\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"f9687e7e73f05576ceae05019fef5f88776dd0be425e6c4d2ca2a270d6048fe4\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize established 2005 history\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d1\"},\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... the Man Booker International Prize, was inaugurated in 2005. Until 2015, it was given every two years to a living author of any nationality for a body of work published in English or generally available in English translation. In 2016, the award was significantly reconfigured, and is now ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2004\\n\\n- Short-listed for the Booker International Prize, 2005\\n\\n- Banff Centre's National Arts Award, 2005\\n\\n- Edinburgh's International Book Festival Enlightenment Award, 2005\\n\\n- Chicago Tribune Literary Prize, 2005\\n\\n- Markets Initiative Order of the Forest, 2006\\n\\n- Short-listed for Booker International Prize, 2007\\n\\n- Winner Blue Metropolis Literary Grand ... \",\"title\":\"https://margaretatwood.ca/awards-recognitions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... Coetzee | Slow Man | Secker & Warburg | *John Sutherland (chair) *Lindsay Duguid *Rick Gekoski *Josephine Hart *David Sexton |\\n| 2005 The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en |archive-date=10 December 2022 |archive-url= |url-status=live }} | Longlist | Rachel Cusk | In the Fold | Faber ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... His last novel, Judas, was shortlisted for the Booker Prize in 2017 and won the Yasnaya Polyana Foreign Fiction Award. He received several international awards, including the Prix Femina, the Israel Prize, the Goethe Prize, the Frankfurt Peace Prize and the 2013 Franz Kafka Prize. He died in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... Prize for Fiction.)\\n* Oryx and Crake (2003, finalist for the 2003 Booker Prize and the 2003 Governor General's Award and shortlisted for the 2004 Orange Prize for Fiction.)\\n* The Penelopiad (2005, nominated for the 2006 Mythopoeic Fantasy Award for Adult Literature and longlisted for the 2007 International ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d70\"},\"ref\":\"d70\",\"snippet\":\" ... Since 2005, a second prize, the International Booker Prize, has also been awarded, which since 2016 has gone to the best work in translation.\\n\\nThese 70 judges were 57 percent men; 75 percent English; 16 percent Irish, Scottish, or Welsh; 10 percent other nationalities; and 99 percent white ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... But in recent months it has gathered momentum, fueled by booksellers and readers, particularly on Twitter, where people have shared their intensely emotional responses.\\\" It soon became a bestseller, first in the UK, where it was longlisted for the Booker Prize, and then in the US.\\n\\nGarth Greenwell ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/a-century-of-reading-the-10-books-that-have-defined-the-2010s-so-far/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... Clarke Award, the Booker Prize, the Center for Fiction First Novel Prize, the Costa First Novel Prize, the Costa Novel Prize, the Dos Passos Prize, the Hugo Award for Best Novel, the IMPAC (now the International Dublin Literary Award), the Kirkus Prize, the LA Times Book Prize, the ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/which-writers-have-won-the-most-major-prizes/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... The decade—and the Australian phase of Carey's career—culminated with the publication of Oscar and Lucinda (1988), which won the Booker McConnell Prize (as it was then known) and brought the author international recognition. Carey explained that the novel was inspired, in part, by his time ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Carey_(novelist)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Previously called the Man Booker Prize, it has been awarded since 1969.\\n\\nRecent Winner\\n\\nPrevious Winner (2023)\\n\\nInternational Booker Prize\\n\\nA counterpart to the Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize was established in 2005. Originally presented biennially, in 2016 it had become an annual occurrence. Awarded to a ... \",\"title\":\"https://rocketexpansion.com/book-awards/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"89c9162b0a980e61db1ab69eb532d07f92edb3a1cee0536267fe41004add2648\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"6daf090253320bbeff6551aca2653f52c285a21a280568721f7143a4b1ee31c8\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize created 2005 2016 reconfigured\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d73\"},\"ref\":\"d73\",\"snippet\":\" ... Bernardine Evaristo\\naudio_read_by: Anna-Maria Nabirye Girl, Woman, Other 2 May 2019 Penguin Books UK 15 October 2019\\ncover_artist: Neil Kenlock (photos)Bernardine Evaristo Girl, Woman, Other 2 May 2019 Penguin Books Limited 978-0-241-98500-7Ali Campbell (design)\\ncountry: United Kingdom\\nlanguage: English ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl,_Woman,_Other\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Girl, Woman, Other by Bernardine Evaristo (2019)\\n\\nBritish author Bernardine Evaristo's eighth novel was also a historic first: the first novel by a Black woman to win the Booker Prize. Not that it should have been a surprise – Girl, Woman, Other is an innovative, experimental novel that ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.penguin.co.uk/discover/articles/books-that-defined-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... Bernardine Evaristo on a childhood shaped by racism: 'I was never going to give up'\\nauthor: Bernardine Evaristo\\ndate: 2021-10-03\\n---\\nWhen I won the Booker prize in 2019 for my novel Girl, Woman, Other, I became an \\\"overnight success\\\", after 40 years working professionally in the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/sep/25/bernardine-evaristo-on-a-childhood-shaped-by-racism-i-was-never-going-to-give-up\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d76\"},\"ref\":\"d76\",\"snippet\":\" ... Bernardine Evaristo\\n\\nAuthor\\n\\n(1959–)\\n\\nBernardine Evaristo is a British author and academic. Her books have been awarded 'Book of the Year' 60 times and her novel Girl, Woman, Other jointly won the Booker Prize in 2019, making her the first Black woman to claim the prize. She has ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.thersa.org/rsa-journal/50-famous-fellows/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... Lincoln in the Bardo - George Saunders (2017) - 10\\n\\nThe Narrow Road to the Deep North - Richard Flanagan (2014) - 9.5\\n\\nGirl, Woman, Other - Bernardine Evaristo (2019) - 9\\n\\nA Brief History of Seven Killings - Marlon James (2015) - 9\\n\\nBring Up The Bodies - Hilary Mantel (2012) - 8.5\\n\\nThe Sense ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Girl, Woman, Other, joint winner 2019 by Bernardine Evaristo This joint 2019 Booker Prize winner follows twelve characters on their personal journeys over the last one hundred years. From Newcastle to Cornwall and the beginning of the twentieth century to the modern day, each of them is searching ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.panmacmillan.com/blogs/literary/our-all-time-favourite-man-booker-prize-winning-novels\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d79\"},\"ref\":\"d79\",\"snippet\":\" ... Potboiler Television, the small-screen wing of Gail Egan and Andrea Calderwood's UK production house, has won rights to Bernardine Evaristo's Booker-winning novel Girl, Woman, Other.\\n\\nThe book, published last year, made Evaristo the first black woman ever to win the Booker Prize. It stayed ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt3781380/news/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d80\"},\"ref\":\"d80\",\"snippet\":\" ... Girl, Woman, Other by Bernardine Evaristo\\n\\nOn opening Girl, Woman, Other, I was immediately struck by the simplicity of its verse form – the text on the page looks like poetry, and it flows too, with line breaks instead of full stops. It is easy to read, easy to ... \",\"title\":\"https://createdtoread.com/category/bookreviews/literary-fiction/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... The other judges were novelist Bernardine Evaristo and journalist Emily Maitlis.\\n\\n\\\"We unanimously agreed that Maurice and Maralyn is a non-fiction work that reaches the highest literary eminence,\\\" Bryson added.\\n\\nThe Nero Book Awards are the successors to the Costa Book Awards and were founded in 2023 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2x0eyr9kjo\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d82\"},\"ref\":\"d82\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2019 The Testaments, a sequel to The Handmaid's Tale, was published to critical acclaim and was a cowinner (with Bernardine Evaristo's Girl, Woman, Other) of the Booker Prize.\\n\\nThe Blind Assassin (2000) is an intricately constructed narrative centering on the memoir of an elderly Canadian ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Margaret-Atwood\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"e5324e6a32e7ec1be85727bb539f75ee94db1f4b603bf2993f05723f0ff6cacd\",\"replay_requested\